 in `.flywheel/review.jsonl` (45 → 55). Correctness and security independently flagged the same ceiling — correlation is per bead, not per run — documented as a `// ponytail:` naming the `(bead, pr)` upgrade since cost lines carry no `pr=` yet. Five accepted and fixed (deduplicated cost block, dead guard, `0 of 0` wording, trimmed comments), two rejected with reasons, two ignored as pre-existing.\n\n**PR:** https://github.com/jamesponwith/agentic-flywheel/pull/69 — open against `main`, `w:2`, not merged. Bead left open with a note; `bead.claimed`/`bead.pr_opened` logged and committed through the PR.\n\n**Left out:** did not run `fleet cost` against the live ledger — the sandbox refused executing the built binary. Unit tests cover the behaviour. Untracked `.flywheel/run-context.json` was left alone as the spawner's file.","ttft_ms":2874,"type":"result","duration_ms":393202,"uuid":"490fa66e-87c0-4629-977f-288c270b3b79","ttft_stream_ms":1850,"time_to_request_ms":109,"queued_turn_count":0}
